## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | js/preCliDevelopmentSetup.js | 🚨 blocking ci gate crap failed — 3 new functions over the crap ratchet red ci on head 363c94ed the crap check failed 0 regression s 3 new over threshold → process completed with exit code 2 per ci failures md text new 8 js preclidevelopmentsetup js resolvelegstartheadsha 8 1 new 8 js preclidevelopmentsetup js postlegstartstatusbesteffort 10 new 8 js unit tests test preclidevelopmentsetup js loadforgh1364 11 1 the ratchet crap threshold 8 crap may only decrease requires lowering cyclomatic complexity or closing the uncovered branches all three functions pass their tests — this is purely the complexity coverage gate and the repo already has the playbook the gh 1363 rework enrichment helpers extracted for the crap ratchet see the exports comment below this block concrete fix paths 1 resolvelegstartheadsha 8 1 — extract isvalidheadsha sha and probefreshheadsha helpers and add the missing mixed path test remembered sha absent invalid → fresh git rev parse head succeeds — currently the only uncovered branch today s tests only hit remembered valid and fallback throws 2 postlegstartstatusbesteffort 10 — extract the guard chain no config provider github no repository scope no sha into a pure resolvelegstartstatustarget config customparams helper in legstartsignal js zero io 100 coverable leaving a small posting path here the config guard is currently untested — add a direct call with config null 3 loadforgh1364 11 1 cov 90 6 — split the globals builder gh1364globals bag opts from the require map builder so each helper s cc and uncovered branches fit under the gate tests themselves are green 875 passed 0 failed run legstartsignal 26 26 and run preclidevelopmentsetup 95 95 verified locally — only the ratchet gate blocks the merge |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | js/common/legStartSignal.js | 💡 suggestion classifier recall — ref race checkout failures land in other instead of checkout the checkout pattern list covers pathspec remote ref transport messages well but misses the failure shape this pipeline can hit when origin devbranch disappears between proberemotebranch and checkoutexistingremotebranch s fallback reset text fatal origin dev proj 1 is not a commit and a branch dev proj 1 cannot be created from it that message matches no pattern → classifies other the environment setup command bucket per the docblock instead of checkout even though it is exactly a ref problem consider adding is not a commit and or cannot be created from to the checkout array signal only impact the leg still stops and the failed status still posts — only the reason class is coarser pure data change in class patterns fully testable in test legstartsignal js |
| F3 | open | SUGGESTION | js/unit-tests/test_workingDir.js | 🪶 nit dead legstartsignal entries in require maps of loaders that never load preclidevelopmentsetup js only js preclidevelopmentsetup js requires common legstartsignal js verified grep rln require legstartsignal js but the mechanical addition also landed in require maps used to load modules that never touch it — makeisolatedconfigloader configloader js the preclitestautomationsetup loaders and the posttestautomationresults loaders in this file makerequire ignores unused map entries so it is harmless — just noise copied along with the already dead legfailurereport neighbor lines optional drop these entries or leave as is for symmetry no behavior change either way |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

# PR Diff Truncated

Original size: 62825 characters.
Kept: first 7800 and last 4200 characters.

The full diff is available in the checked-out PR branch. Use `git diff` or CodeGraph for focused source navigation instead of relying only on this file.

```diff
diff --git a/js/common/legStartSignal.js b/js/common/legStartSignal.js
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..90bdf66ef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/js/common/legStartSignal.js
@@ -0,0 +1,214 @@
+/**
+ * legStartSignal.js — the leg-start phase signal builder (gh-1364).
+ *
+ * A dev leg answers, machine-readably, the question "can agent legs currently
+ * start work on this main SHA?". In the 2026-11-04 outage every leg died in
+ * the setup phase, but the only way to know ALL failures were setup-phase was
+ * to open run logs by hand. Every leg already crosses the setup boundary —
+ * now it emits the signal there:
+ *
+ *   1. ALWAYS one summary line in the leg log at the setup boundary:
+ *        `leg-start: ok (branch <name>)`  — setup crossed, the dev branch is ready
+ *        `leg-start: failed (<reason-class>: <first error line>)` — setup died
+ *   2. BEST-EFFORT commit status on the head SHA the leg ran against:
+ *        `leg-start/ok`     (state success, description: branch name)
+ *        `leg-start/failed` (state failure, description: reason class)
+ *   3. Reason classes are a CLOSED set, not free text:
+ *        `git-state` — dirty/untracked workspace blocking checkout
+ *        `checkout`  — ref/fetch problems (pathspec, missing remote ref, …)
+ *        `config`    — invalid customParams/config/hook wiring
+ *        `other`     — anything else (e.g. environment setup commands)
+ *
+ * Acting on the signal (gating dispatch, parking) is OUT of scope — the
+ * analyzer/SM policy reads it; this module only emits.
+ *
+ * Structure (mirrors legFailureReport.js):
+ *   - every function is PURE — GraalJS-clean (var + plain functions),
+ *     JSON-safe data, zero requires;
